### Design rationale
| Decision | Why |
|---|---|
| Placed **immediately after Export** | Same mental model ("get the chat out"), so users scan one group instead of hunting |
| `fa-bug` + `text-warning` | Destructive-adjacent, not destructive: signals "raw internals", not "delete". Reads at a glance even without the label |
| **Not** hidden in `channelMode` | A group conversation is exactly the kind of thread that needs a postmortem |
| `v-if="canDump"` **not** `disabled` | Hidden beats a disabled button with no explanation — non-admins never see a locked mystery |
| Label kept in the sidebar (unlike the header's icon-only) | The sidebar is a text list; an icon-only row there reads as a toolbar and breaks the vertical rhythm |

**Anti-patterns to avoid:** putting dump inside the existing `ExportChat` dialog (postmortem data must not be mixed into the shareable export), and gating it in the sidebar with its own role check (two sources of truth for permissions — the host decides, children render).

